WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:01.830
- [Narrator] If you think of blight,

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.810
you probably don't picture something

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.520
like this parking garage,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.190
but New York considers it blighted.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.660
That's because blight is a word

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.510
with more than just a
negative connotation.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:15.270
It has the power to
unlock billions of dollars

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:18.030
for real estate development
by opening the door

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:22.530
for governments to seize
private property for public use.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.050
Just look at New York's $40 billion plan

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:30.050
for Penn Station or LA's $2
billion Angels Landing project.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:33.210
Even Seattle's famous
Pike Place was transformed

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:37.140
from this to this on the basis of blight.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.000
- It can be the basis for deciding

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.600
that the area should be
condemned and redeveloped.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.030
- [Narrator] But these
redevelopment projects don't hinge

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:48.840
on the same interpretation
of blight, just the word.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.510
Here's why blight is so tough to define,

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.670
how it's used to redevelop cities,

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.823
and why its use is a
source of heated debate.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:01.680
Blight has been blamed for
increasing crime, drug use

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.270
and unsanitary conditions

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.460
in neighborhoods across the country

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:09.360
but the standard isn't the
same across every legal code.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.250
Take Pittsburgh as an example.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.290
Here blight could be a building used

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.600
for an immoral purpose.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.860
In Columbus, Kansas,
foot-tall weeds check the box.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.920
In Washington State, being
a menace to the public

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.860
was the rationale used
to classify this motel

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.350
as blighted in 2015.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:32.340
- What is your standard that
you use to determine blight?

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:36.750
- Blight, it's a difficult
term to define precisely

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.910
because it's used in a
lot of different ways.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:42.420
- Amy Lavine specializes in
land use and municipal law.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.710
- She has exceptional knowledge

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.720
in the area of eminent domain

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.720
and was integral in
drafting our legislation.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.020
- In general, it's used
to identify the land

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.480
that should be part of
a redevelopment area.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.360
- [Narrator] And once land
is identified as blighted,

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.970
the stage is set for eminent domain,

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:03.180
giving the government the
power to seize the property.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:07.260
- If the government needs to
build a school or build a road,

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.420
they can go in and they can take property

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.220
from private property owners

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.400
and then use it to provide
those public purposes.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.020
- [Narrator] New York and the agency

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.030
in charge of the Penn Station project,

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:21.030
Empire State Development,
are using eminent domain

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.730
after deeming these blocks as blighted,

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.830
the conclusion of a neighborhood study.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.930
in the spring of 2020.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:30.570
Some of what Empire State
Development called blighted

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.160
includes this building

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.830
with its missing windows, cracked curbs

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:37.590
and ADA inaccessibility.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.150
This white storefront was cited

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:43.680
for its stained windows,
scaffolding and cracked sidewalks.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.100
- Empire State Development
needs to meet certain conditions

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.350
to be involved in a project

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.870
and they do that by making a finding

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:55.410
that the property is
substandard and insanitary.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.750
- [Narrator] Then the state
can slate the buildings

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:00.210
for redevelopment using eminent domain.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:04.290
- This Penn Station
development is crucial for us.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:05.550
- [Narrator] On these eight lots,

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.070
the state is proposing new skyscrapers,

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.560
which it says will help
fund major improvements

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.700
to Penn Station,

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.030
as well as cosmetic upgrades
like cleaning up these drains

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:17.490
and the stained walls.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:18.960
But governments across the US

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:21.660
have used eminent domain for decades.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.980
Just look at Seattle.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.450
In the late 1950s,

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:27.660
city officials started
declaring neighborhoods blighted

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.220
and began redevelopment.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.510
- Your city is engaged in
dramatically revitalizing several

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.160
of our older neighborhoods.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.470
- [Narrator] Some residents
said blight designations

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:40.620
targeted low income
neighborhoods and minorities.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.920
That project faced opposition
back when it started.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:47.100
In a letter, one resident
called it "grossly unfair,"

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:50.430
and almost 60 years later,
Seattle passed a resolution

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.460
on how the forced acquisition
of a church property,

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.560
which occurred as part of that project

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:57.570
heard the local Black community.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.450
Today that land is part of a city park.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.570
- A lot of people think
that urban renewal is over

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:04.890
and not still happening,

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.170
and so they call them different things.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.030
In the case of Barclays Center,

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:13.530
or Penn Station, it's
economic redevelopment.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.630
- [Narrator] And relocation still occurs.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.090
These are all the businesses
that might be displaced

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.038
by the Penn Station project.

00:04:20.038 --> 00:04:22.680
It's the main reason
why some people living

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:25.800
and working in the Penn
Station area are opposed.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.370
Although relocated residents
are given just compensation

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.460
or fair market value for their property.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:34.380
- I think people do, in a lot of cases,

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:37.050
get the sense that the basis

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:40.890
for the condemnation is
a little bit subjective.

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:42.930
- [Narrator] Residents in
the Penn area are responding

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:47.040
in similar ways as Seattle
residents, 80 years later.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.110
One lawyer even filed a lawsuit

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:51.450
to urge New York to
disclose communications

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.670
with real estate developer Vornado,

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:56.790
the largest private
stakeholder in the project.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:00.090
One watchdog group estimated
that Vornado may receive up

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:03.870
to $1.2 billion in subsidies
during the project.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.540
Vornado declined to comment.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.803
Empire State Development said

00:05:07.803 --> 00:05:10.320
that Hochul's proposal is what New Yorkers

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.330
and Penn Station deserve.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.460
- So the main part of the lawsuit,

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.500
it is about the issue of blight.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.650
The way the law is set up doesn't
make it particularly easy.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:21.660
- [Narrator] A government's
ability to use blight

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.990
to seize property has been
challenged in the past.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:28.800
One case even reached the
Supreme Court in 2005,

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.050
which held that governments
can take property

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:34.350
for the purpose of promoting
economic development.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.720
- Economic development is a traditional

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:39.330
and long-accepted function of government,

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.330
- [Narrator] As construction
begins in the Penn Station area

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.733
so will the legal cases against it.

00:05:44.733 --> 00:05:47.400
(pensive music)

